.TH BURNRECON 1 "2026-08-10" "Burn Suite 1.2" "Burn Suite Manual"
.SH NAME
burnrecon \- automated OSINT reconnaissance tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 ./burnrecon.py
.RI [ target ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B burnrecon
.RI [ target ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI "  (if installed via " install.sh )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B burnrecon
runs a reconnaissance sweep against a domain, IP, or company name and
writes a report. It is
.B passive by default \-
it queries only third\-party OSINT sources (WHOIS, certificate
transparency, passive DNS, IP geolocation, Shodan, ASN data, email\-auth
records, Hunter.io, HaveIBeenPwned) and never sends packets to the
target's own infrastructure.
.PP
The
.B \-\-active
flag additionally probes the target directly (HTTP header and TLS
certificate grab, CORS test, DNS zone\-transfer attempt, subdomain\-takeover
checks, web\-metadata fetch, and a quick nmap port scan).
The
.B \-\-aggressive
flag adds loud techniques on top (DNS subdomain brute\-force and a full
top\-1000 scripted port scan); it implies \fB\-\-active\fR.
.PP
It analyzes the gathered data for actionable findings (missing security
headers, weak/missing SPF and DMARC, risky open ports, TLS problems, an
allowed zone transfer, dangling\-CNAME takeovers, an expiring domain,
known CVEs from Shodan) and writes a plain\-text and/or JSON report.
.PP
Does not require root.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B dig (dnsutils)
Required for DNS record, DMARC, zone\-transfer, and takeover lookups. Skipped gracefully if missing.
.TP
.B whois
Required for WHOIS lookups. Skipped gracefully if missing.
.TP
.B nmap
Required for the port scan (active/aggressive). Skipped gracefully if missing.
.TP
.B python3\-requests
Required for crt.sh, passive DNS, ipapi.co, RIPEstat, Shodan, Hunter, and HIBP lookups.
.TP
.B python3\-cryptography
Optional. Enables full parsing of TLS certificates that fail validation
(SANs, exact expiry, signature algorithm) instead of just the failure
reason. Degrades gracefully if missing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I target
Domain, IP, or company name. If omitted, the tool prompts interactively.
.TP
.B \-\-active
Enable active probes (HTTP/TLS grab, CORS, zone transfer, takeover,
web\-metadata, quick port scan) in addition to the passive OSINT.
.TP
.B \-\-aggressive
Enable active plus aggressive techniques (DNS brute\-force, full
top\-1000 scripted port scan). Implies \fB\-\-active\fR.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fR{txt,json,both}
Report format. Default \fBtxt\fR. \fBboth\fR writes a .txt and a .json.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Write reports into \fIDIR\fR instead of the default \fIburn_report/\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-portscan
Skip the nmap port scan even in active/aggressive mode.
.TP
.B \-\-wordlist \fIFILE\fR
Custom wordlist for \fB\-\-aggressive\fR DNS brute\-force.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-file \fIFILE\fR
Batch mode: read one target per line from \fIFILE\fR; each gets its own report.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Reduce console output (errors are still shown).
.SH USAGE
.TP
.B Passive (default):
\fBpython3 ./burnrecon.py example.com\fR
.TP
.B Active, both report formats:
\fBpython3 ./burnrecon.py example.com \-\-active \-o both\fR
.TP
.B Aggressive:
\fBpython3 ./burnrecon.py example.com \-\-aggressive\fR
.PP
IP\-only targets skip subdomain enumeration, email\-format guessing, DMARC,
zone transfer, and DNS brute\-force (not applicable). A report is written to
\fIburn_report/burnrecon_<timestamp>.{txt,json}\fR.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS Shodan API key
Shodan intelligence is optional and requires a free API key from
.BR https://shodan.io .
Each user must supply their own key. Copy the template
\fIshodan_api.txt.example\fR to \fIshodan_api.txt\fR (in the same folder
as \fBburnrecon.py\fR), then replace the placeholder with your key \- no
quotes, just the key itself:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cp shodan_api.txt.example shodan_api.txt
.EE
.RE
.PP
The script reads it automatically at startup; if the file is missing or
empty, Shodan lookups are skipped with a diagnostic code rather than
failing. \fIshodan_api.txt\fR is git\-ignored so a personal key is never
committed or shared.
.SS Hunter.io and HaveIBeenPwned keys
Two further optional OSINT sources use the same pattern. Copy
\fIhunter_api.txt.example\fR to \fIhunter_api.txt\fR for Hunter.io email
enrichment, and \fIhibp_api.txt.example\fR to \fIhibp_api.txt\fR for
HaveIBeenPwned breach lookups, pasting your own key into each. Both files
are git\-ignored; if absent, those lookups are skipped with a diagnostic
code.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Recon has no fatal error paths once started \- it always completes and
writes a report, even if every individual module fails or finds nothing;
missing dependencies and empty results are recorded as diagnostic codes
instead of stopping the run. The tool exits non\-zero only for a usage
error before the scan begins (e.g. no target given, or an unreadable
\fB\-\-file\fR).
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Every failure, skip, or empty result is logged to the console and to
the report's DIAGNOSTICS section as a \fBRECON\-NNN\fR code. See
.I ERROR_CODES.txt
in the suite root for the full reference \- e.g. "no DNS records found"
(a real result) is a distinct code from "dig isn't installed" (an
environment gap), so the two are never conflated in a report.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I burn_report/burnrecon_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt
Generated report for each run.
.TP
.I burn_report/burnrecon_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.json
Generated JSON report (with \fB\-o json\fR or \fB\-o both\fR).
.TP
.I shodan_api.txt, hunter_api.txt, hibp_api.txt
Optional API keys, read at startup. Each is git\-ignored.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.B FOR AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY.
Only investigate domains/targets you own or have explicit written
permission to investigate.
.PP
The default mode is passive \- no packets are sent to the target's own
infrastructure, only queries to third\-party OSINT services. The
.B \-\-active
and
.B \-\-aggressive
flags DO contact the target directly (HTTP/TLS connections, DNS zone\-transfer
attempts, and nmap port scans; brute\-force under \fB\-\-aggressive\fR). Use
them only within the scope of your authorization. No exploitation or
credential attacks are performed in any mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
